# ─── Storefront proxy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drop product pages are server-rendered by the ARK app on Railway, but they must
# be SERVED from this apex domain, because that is where the site's search
# authority lives. Every drop page's canonical tag already says
# arkscreenprinting.com/shop/<slug>; these two rules are what make that URL real.
#
# Status 200 makes it a REWRITE, not a redirect: the visitor and Googlebot both
# see the apex URL in the address bar and never learn the app subdomain exists.
# A 301 here would hand the authority straight back to the subdomain and defeat
# the point.
#
# The trailing "!" is force, which makes these win over any static file that might
# later be added at /shop. Nothing shadows them today.
#
# Both lines are needed: "/shop/*" does not reliably match the bare "/shop", and
# bare /shop is the storefront hub — the only URL in the drop sitemap and the
# target of every drop page's breadcrumb.
#
# Rollback: delete this file. The pages keep working on the subdomain.

/shop      https://design.arkscreenprinting.com/shop         200!
/shop/*    https://design.arkscreenprinting.com/shop/:splat   200!
